# Per-copy SLR caps. A class copy is placed whole in an SLR where it can; one
# past every SLR's memory or logic is cut by the placer, its wide state and
# store ports then crossing SLLs (r16c, 11-07: a slice copy of 517 URAM
# against SLRs of 496 / 511 / 204 failed partitioning at 23,987 SLLs).
#
# The planner (foldsim_degree state --copy-cap): each copy's URAM and RAMB36
# are pools of the storage choice, capped at one SLR's with the margin: two
# wide, shallow memories both in URAM without the cap, one moved under it;
# the SLR by name or the smallest. With --copy-cap-luts the copy's LUTs
# (its logic plus its stores' LUTs and LUTRAM, over the placed / priced LUTs,
# 1.15) and its stores' flops too: LUTRAM stores move to
# block RAM when the copy would outgrow the SLR. copy_sites with the schedule: a paged copy
# keeps its registers in page RAMs, not a distributed RAM an instance deep.
# RUN: python3 %S/Inputs/slr-copy-cap/model.py %foldsim_tools/foldsim.py | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MODEL
# MODEL: no cap: {{\[\['ultra'\], \['ultra'\]\]}} uram 176.0 bram 0.0
# MODEL: cap: {{\['distributed', 'ultra'\]}} copy uram 88.0 copy bram 0.0 cap 100.0
# MODEL: no lut cap: {{\['distributed', 'distributed'\]}}
# MODEL: lut cap: {{\['block', 'block'\]}} copy luts 500000 cap 520000.0
# MODEL: smallest {'name': 'B', 'uram': 1.0, 'bram': 4.0} A {'name': 'A', 'uram': 10.0, 'bram': 20.0}
# MODEL: luts {'name': 'A', 'uram': 10.0, 'bram': 20.0, 'lut': 43.4{{[0-9]+}}, 'lutram': 21.7{{[0-9]+}}, 'ff': 100.0}
# MODEL: copy sites: unscheduled {{[0-9]+}}, paged {{[0-9]+}}, paged smaller True
# MODEL: read buffers: block lutram 114 comb True
# MODEL: off: block lutram 0.0

# The check of a generated netlist (foldsim_sll_check.py, resources counted on
# the netlist; logic within each SLR's capacity times the margin, memories
# within its whole count): the leaf's memory in URAM (64 x 8: a whole
# URAM288) fits only the SLR that has URAM: OK where a copy may take any SLR
# (the copy there), REFUSE (exit 1) where it must fit the other; within SLRs
# of 100 URAM it fits either. Without a placement model in the region the
# SLLs are not projected.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/Inputs/storage
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/x --static --copies Leaf:1 --storage 'Leaf:mem=ultra' Leaf 2> %t/x.log
# RUN: python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_sll_check.py %t/x --log %t/x.log --slr-region %S/Inputs/slr-copy-cap/region-small.json --foldsim-opt foldsim-opt --out %t/any | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ANY
# RUN: not python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_sll_check.py %t/x --log %t/x.log --slr-region %S/Inputs/slr-copy-cap/region-small.json --foldsim-opt foldsim-opt --copy-cap SLR1 --out %t/small | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SMALL
# RUN: python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_sll_check.py %t/x --log %t/x.log --slr-region %S/Inputs/slr-copy-cap/region-big.json --foldsim-opt foldsim-opt --copy-cap smallest --out %t/big | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BIG
# ANY: SLR1 capacity: lut 50,000, lutram 50,000, ff 100,000, uram 0.0, bram 100.0
# ANY: copy cap: any (SLR1, SLR0)
# ANY: Leaf: lut {{[0-9,]+}}, lutram {{[0-9,]+}}, ff {{[0-9,]+}}, uram 1.0, bram 0.0; of each SLR's capacity (binding resource): SLR1 inf %, SLR0 50 %
# ANY: slr1 ({{[0-9]+}} sites): Leaf
# ANY: SLR0 as placed: {{.*}} uram 1.0 (50 %)
# ANY: x: OK: an assignment within the SLRs (no placement model in the region: SLLs not projected)
# SMALL: copy cap: SLR1 (SLR1)
# SMALL: x: REFUSE: Leaf fits no SLR whole (the nearest, SLR1: over its uram)
# BIG: copy cap: smallest (SLR1)
# BIG: x: OK

# The placement model (region-place.json: SLRs of 150 LUTs filled to 75 %):
# the leaf copy (no whole-copy cap) is larger than an SLR's room, so it is
# cut, filling its SLR's room and the rest in the other; its own cut by Rent's
# rule, the links between the sides and the simulator level's constant are
# the boundary's SLLs, a warning over the budget's 30.
# RUN: python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_sll_check.py %t/x --log %t/x.log --slr-region %S/Inputs/slr-copy-cap/region-place.json --foldsim-opt foldsim-opt --copy-cap none --out %t/place | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLACE
# PLACE: (no whole assignment: Leaf left out, spread over the room the others leave)
# PLACE: the design over the region: lut 69 %, lutram 24 %, ff 61 % (placement fill lut 75 %, lutram 75 %, ff 75 %)
# PLACE: SLR1 as placed: lut 112 (75 %)
# PLACE: Leaf cut over the SLRs: SLR1 58 %, SLR0 42 % of its logic
# PLACE: boundary SLR1-SLR0: 22 SLLs projected (links 2, cut copies 19, simulator level and kernel 1)
# PLACE: x: WARN: 22 SLLs projected over SLR1-SLR0 (budget 30); Leaf cut over SLRs

# Netlist resources are mandatory: without the generation's foldsim_sim.mlir
# the check refuses (the schedule's estimates miss stage registers, read
# buffers and the simulator level); --resources schedule is an estimate,
# never a verdict.
# RUN: mkdir -p %t/nonet && cp %t/x/schedule.txt %t/nonet/
# RUN: not python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_sll_check.py %t/nonet --log %t/x.log --slr-region %S/Inputs/slr-copy-cap/region-place.json --foldsim-opt foldsim-opt --out %t/nn | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NONET
# NONET: nonet: REFUSE: no netlist ({{.*}}foldsim_sim.mlir missing)
# RUN: python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_sll_check.py %t/x --log %t/x.log --slr-region %S/Inputs/slr-copy-cap/region-place.json --resources schedule --foldsim-opt foldsim-opt --out %t/sched | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SCHED
# SCHED: resources from the schedule (AN ESTIMATE ONLY
# SCHED: x: ESTIMATE (schedule resources, not a verdict)

# The driver's --sll-check runs the check on the netlist it generated
# (<out>/sll/sll.txt) and fails on a refusal.
# RUN: not foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/d --static --copies Leaf:1 --storage 'Leaf:mem=ultra' --slr-region %S/Inputs/slr-copy-cap/region-place.json --sll-check Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DRV
# DRV: foldsim: SLL check: d: REFUSE: Leaf fits no SLR whole
# DRV: --sll-check refuses this netlist
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DRVR < %t/d/sll/sll.txt
# DRVR: d: REFUSE: Leaf fits no SLR whole
